  "summary": "CONSENT at 0 MUST-FIX and 0 SHOULD-FIX. D-154 lawfully packages D-149's fifth and last proposed later work as one three-limb act: scoped D-002 required-gate-set succession, same-act D-086 harness naming, and exact MF-6 file-08 mutation. G28 is free because the live table ends at G27. The before operand occurs exactly once; the new row is one valid eight-cell row; and an in-memory application produces 28 gate rows, 28/28 owners, 24/24 required names, 25 OPEN and 3 HARD-BLOCKED while condition 4 stays MET. The row's combined claim, corpus, owner, and pass threshold match DR-131 NT-7/NT-8 only: the host does not mint fail/warn outside core policyOutcome and does not mint a D9 class, exit, or HostTermination from policyOutcome; it maps only existing D9 v1.14 classes. After G28, every DR-131 NT class has a named execution remainder, so D-056 gates 2/3 hold for those classes. The act still does not establish gate 1's application-grade/no-express-reservation limb or perform gate 4's dedicated SATISFIED-grade cycle, and therefore does not make DR-131 eligible in kind. It marks nothing SATISFIED, opens no Class A, does not use CANDIDATE-NOT-APPLIED as an eligibility bar, restores neither G17 nor G13, invents no D9 code, changes no other D-018 item-2 set, and authorizes no implementation. Custody and cited digests hold.",
